7 Distribution images
*********************

7.1 Host dependency installation
================================

Host requirements and workspace baseline packages are separate.  These
commands cover core rootless tools and optional age backup tools; doctor
prints only packages missing for each feature.  Run OS package commands
manually with the privileges appropriate to your machine (‘sudo’ on a
configured regular host, or as root without sudo in an administrative
shell).

| Host distro | Core rootless prerequisites plus optional backup tools |
| -- | -- | | Tumbleweed | ‘sudo zypper refresh && sudo zypper install
python3 podman passt shadow catatonit conmon crun age’ | | Leap | ‘sudo
zypper refresh && sudo zypper install python3 podman passt shadow
catatonit conmon runc age’ | | Ubuntu / Debian | ‘sudo apt update &&
sudo apt install python3 podman passt uidmap catatonit conmon crun age’
| | Fedora | ‘sudo dnf install python3 podman passt shadow-utils
catatonit conmon crun age’ | | Arch | ‘sudo pacman -Syu --needed python
podman passt shadow catatonit conmon crun age’ | | Alpine | ‘sudo apk
add python3 podman passt shadow-subids catatonit conmon crun age’ |

Installing packages alone does not configure subordinate IDs, cgroups,
or make rootful Podman rootless.  Alpine requires its release's
community repository for some providers; Ubuntu may require its official
universe repository.  Use a current supported OS with Python 3.10+ and
pasta-capable Podman; an older Leap/ Python combination may need an OS
upgrade rather than a package reinstall.

| Feature | Host dependencies | | -- | -- | | Launch/reset/sync | Linux,
running Python 3.10+, Podman, pasta (‘passt’), newuidmap/newgidmap,
catatonit, conmon, crun or runc, host OpenCode 1.x or 2.x | |
Maintenance/stop/repair/purge | Linux, Python, Podman and UID helpers;
history preservation/deletion additionally uses host OpenCode | |
Full/portable backup | Linux, Python, rootless Podman/UID helpers,
age/age-keygen (both from ‘age’), memfd support | | Backup inspection |
Linux, Python, age/age-keygen, memfd; no Podman/OpenCode/vault extra | |
Restore | Backup prerequisites plus pasta, init/helper/runtime providers
for container creation | | Optional vault | ‘cryptography’ in the same
Python environment as oc-box; no age requirement | | GitHub
installation/upgrade | Git and Python; one-line download also needs
curl, mktemp and trusted CA certificates | | Storage reports | GNU ‘du’
from ‘coreutils’; BusyBox du is insufficient; other metrics still work
if absent | | FUSE overlay driver | ‘fuse-overlayfs’ only if
selected/needed; kernel overlay does not require it | | Read manuals |
man (‘man’, ‘man-db’, or Alpine ‘mandoc’) and info (‘info’ or ‘texinfo’)
| | Regenerate manuals | GNU makeinfo (‘texinfo’); contributor-only,
never required to install/use oc-box |

Host OpenCode is not supplied by these mappings; see
https://opencode.ai/docs/#install.  Use the existing Python installation
channel for vault support: ‘uv tool install --force 'oc-box[vault]'’,
‘pipx inject oc-box 'cryptography>=44'’, or GitHub/source
‘--with-vault’.  Do not install Python dependencies into system Python
to fix an isolated tool's missing extra.

Inside each workspace, oc-box automatically installs Bash, CA
certificates, curl, Git, Python, ripgrep, tar/gzip, Node/npm, and PDF
tools (‘poppler-tools’ on openSUSE, ‘poppler-utils’ on
Debian/Ubuntu/Fedora/Alpine, ‘poppler’ on Arch).  uv/uvx and matching
OpenCode are bootstrapped inside private storage.  MCPs, formatters,
language servers, plugins and project libraries may have their own
requirements; doctor does not infer those from project configuration.

Distro CI installs mapped packages in disposable instances of all seven
catalog images, checks actual command providers, tests standard age, and
verifies scoped guidance.  It does not run nested rootless Podman or
replace host lifecycle tests.

     Name         Image
     tumbleweed   registry.opensuse.org/opensuse/tumbleweed:latest
     leap         registry.opensuse.org/opensuse/leap:latest
     ubuntu       docker.io/library/ubuntu:24.04
     debian       docker.io/library/debian:stable
     fedora       registry.fedoraproject.org/fedora:latest
     arch         docker.io/library/archlinux:base
     alpine       docker.io/library/alpine:latest

Aliases: ‘opensuse’ and ‘opensuse-tumbleweed’ select ‘tumbleweed’;
‘opensuse-leap’ selects ‘leap’; ‘archlinux’ selects ‘arch’.  ‘oc-box
distros’ reports the actual compiled catalog.  Images are pulled when
missing, not automatically refreshed to a newer remote tag on every
launch.


