13 Exit status
**************

‘0’ means successful informational/lifecycle work or normal TUI exit.  A
TUI launch normally returns OpenCode/Podman's exit code.  oc-box
validation, backend, setup, and sync failures return ‘1’; a successful
TUI followed by failed history sync also returns ‘1’ and retains
container data.  Argument syntax errors return ‘2’.  A Python
KeyboardInterrupt handled by the launcher returns ‘130’.  An exception
during final cleanup can also cause a nonzero result.

Warnings about host devices/SELinux do not themselves make creation
fail.  Podman/driver errors still propagate.  A nonzero status is not
permission to purge data; recover or inspect the existing environment
first.


